From a4f6642ca4ed4684215a7315b72f929d0b342824 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Spree <hello@spreecommerce.org>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 16:21:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add social login to the storefront

WeChat, Douyin and Google sign-in now appear on the login and
registration pages, driven by the store's configured providers.

A provider redirects the browser back to a callback route that
exchanges the code server-side and writes the session into the same
httpOnly cookies password login uses. Providers that return no email
get one completion screen, which creates the account through the API's
registration step. The state the API signed is kept in a cookie and
re-checked before the exchange, and the shopper's destination survives
the round trip.
